GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_DesignTradeoffs> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_DesignTradeoffs> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#DesignTradeoffs> ;
    narr:childCount "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "6a9c720473f9540d5ad542f2925d90f61d74241f" ;
    narr:narration """This region holds a delivery-routing trade-off, all dated to a single ruling window, now joined by a newer cadence question. The chosen approach is [one bundle per run per person rather than one message per skill](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2), with the bundle's close condition fixed as [the run closing, late skills waiting for the next run rather than sending on their own](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4). The rejected alternative stays expandable: [per-skill delivery with client-side collapsing, which moves the ordering problem onto the reader](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5). The choice was contested in the record itself — [a pushback on the batching window, held against](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3) — so the dissent is retrievable beside the verdict. The parent frame states the aim as [shielding recipients from fragmentation](narr:Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling). A newer child opens a distinct question — [recurring reaction summaries scheduled across multi-day windows alongside per-run bundles](narr:Position_WeeklyReactionRollUpCadence) — extending the region from one decision point toward a cadence dimension.""" ;
    narr:reaction """Nothing moved for this hub: the children are the same set the prior digest covered, and the prior narration already carried the [multi-day cadence question](narr:Position_WeeklyReactionRollUpCadence) alongside the [per-run bundle ruling](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2). The narration below re-derives it unchanged.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_WeeklyReactionRollUpCadence> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "we route every reaction through one bundle per run per person, not one\n> message per skill — a person should get one thing to read, not four" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Tanya held: the bundle closes when\nthe run closes, and a skill that misses the close waits for the next run rather\nthan sending on its own." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "The alternative considered and rejected was per-skill\ndelivery with client-side collapsing, which moves the ordering problem onto the\nreader." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Tina pushed back on the batching window" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Reaction delivery bundles strictly per run per person to shield recipients from fragmentation" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_ReactionDeliveryBundling> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The ruling was contested in the record: a pushback on the batching window was raised and held against, so the dissent sits beside the verdict rather than beneath it." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The rejected alternative — per-skill delivery with client-side collapsing — remains retrievable, trading fragmentation for pushing the ordering problem onto the reader." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "A newer cadence question — multi-day recurring summaries alongside per-run bundles — is open, not folded into the per-run ruling." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_WeeklyReactionRollUpCadence> ] ;
    narr:writer "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:nitro" .
}